      "side": 0,
      "message": "Example call stack:\n\nThread1:\nandroid_setup\n-\u003e got cdev  (cdev may be become null here, but will be return if cdev is null)\n-\u003e got gi by container_of\n-\u003e pause due to spin_lock_irqsave\n-\u003e cdev become null  (cdev is derived from the struct gadget_info（\u0026gi-\u003ecdev）, so cdev will not be become null here)\n\nThread2:\nconfigfs_composite_bind\n-\u003e hold spin_lock_irqsave\n-\u003e set_gadget_data(gadget, NULL);  \n ( This line of code only set gadget-\u003edev-\u003ep-\u003edriver_data to NULL,\n   does not change the pointer of the \u0026gi-\u003ecdev.\n\n   set cdev code:\n   struct usb_composite_dev *cdev \u003d \u0026gi-\u003ecdev;\n   set_gadget_data(gadget, cdev); \n     dev-\u003ep-\u003edriver_data \u003d cdev\n \n   set NULL code:\n   set_gadget_data(gadget, NULL); \n     dev-\u003ep-\u003edriver_data \u003d NULL\n\n  so set_gadget_data(gadget, NULL) does not change to the pointer of \"\u0026gi-\u003ecdev\" \n \n-\u003e spin_unlock_irqrestore",
