      "side": 0,
      "message": "Sorry for the mistake. \n\nI mean cdev would be NULL by calling get_gadget_data again in the comment above. After your change, cdev is valid, but get_gadget_data(gadget) could be NULL if another thread calls set_gadget_data(gadget, NULL). Therefore, if you don\u0027t include the if statement check, the kernel will panic in composite_setup(), where cdev is accessed by calling get_gadget_data(gadget) again.\n\nTherefore, I suggest to keep these to avoid kernel panic.",
      "parentUuid": "7b889c38_ef0a929f",
      "revId": "75f82c6a15c4188cbb32825892fc6ae3e95479f0",
